==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|enm}} {{term|revolven||to change direction|lang=enm}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|revolver||to reflect upon|lang=fro}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|revolvere|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|revolvo|revolvō|turn over, roll back, reflect upon|lang=la}} < {{term|re-||back|lang=la}} + {{term|volvo|volvō|roll|lang=la}}; see [[voluble]], [[volve]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|revolves|revolving|revolved}}

# To orbit a central point.
#: ''The Earth '''revolves''' around the sun.''
# To turn on an axis.
#: ''The Earth '''revolves''' once every twenty-four hours.''
# To recur in cycles.
#: ''The program '''revolves''' through all the queues before returning to the start.''
# To [[ponder]] on.

